class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* oddEvenList(ListNode* head) {
        if(head==nullptr || head->next==nullptr){return head;}
        ListNode * odd=head;
        ListNode * even=head->next;
        ListNode *evenStart=even;

        while(even!=NULL&&even->next!=NULL){
            odd->next=even->next;
            odd=odd->next;
            even->next=odd->next;
            even=even->next;
        }
        odd->next=evenStart;
        return head;
    }
};



EXPLANATION:
Create two pointers:
One for odd-position nodes.
One for even-position nodes.
Save the first even node.
This is required to connect the even list at the end.
Traverse the linked list.
Connect each odd node to the next odd-position node.
Move the odd pointer to the next odd node.
Connect each even node to the next even-position node.
Move the even pointer to the next even node.
Repeat these steps until there are no more odd or even nodes.
After the traversal, connect the last odd node to the first even node.
Return the head of the modified linked list.

Time Complexity: O(n) (each node is visited once)

Space Complexity: O(1) (only a few pointers are used)
